'''HURID-327''' was a [[Loadlifter droid (model)|loadlifter droid]] who worked as groundskeeper and luggage porter for [[Pirate Queen]] [[Maz Kanata]]'s [[Takodana Castle|castle]] on the [[planet]] [[Takodana]]. He was jovial and slightly lazy, but kept the area around the castle clear of [[Plant|undergrowth]]. In [[382 BBY]], the [[droid]] witnessed a fight break out in the castle between the [[Galactic Antipiracy Command|lawman]] [[Raf Thatchburn]] argue with Kanata's employee [[Alak]] before Kanata broke it up.

After the [[Aloxian]] [[Youngling|infant]] [[Qort]] was delivered to Kanata's doorstep, HURID-327 tried to calm the child, but the baby instead ripped off the droid's arm and beat the droid to pieces with it. After a [[vonduun crab]] [[Bone|skull]] calmed Qort's violent tendencies, HURID-327 was tickling the infant in the castle when the baby began using [[the Force]], leading to Qort joining the [[Jedi Order]]. In [[34 ABY]], HURID-327 passed the [[human]]s [[Han Solo]], [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], [[Finn]], and the [[BB-series astromech droid|astromech droid]] [[BB-8]] while the groundskeeper walked away from the castle toward its [[starship]]. The castle was then [[Battle of Takodana|destroyed]] by the [[First Order]].

==Biography==
===High Republic Era===
{{Quote|Ah, Dexy Jet! You should've told me you were coming! I would've had ''HURID'' prep a spread of your favorite tasty treats.|Maz Kanata|<ref name="HRA1">[[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 1|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 1]]</ref>}}
[[File:HURID-2022THRA1.png|thumb|left|300px|HURID-327 was employed at Maz Kanata's castle.]]
HURID-327,<ref name="BR2D268" /> also refered to as just HURID,<ref name="HRA1" /> was a [[Loadlifter droid (model)|loadlifter droid]]<ref name="TFAVD" /> that was employed by the [[Pirate Queen]] [[Maz Kanata]]<ref name="Geektionary" /> to work as the groundskeeper and lugage porter of her [[Takodana Castle|castle]] on the [[planet]] [[Takodana]], which was also its permenant residence.<ref name="AA">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> His duties included keeping the area around the castle and the paths that led to it clear of intrusive [[Plant|undergrowth]]<ref name="BR2D268" /> and any heavy-weight work<ref name="Geektionary" /> such as carrying larger items of luggage for select guests at the castle.<ref name="BR2D268" /> The loadlifter also helped to enforce Kanata's rules and attending to her guests needs.<ref name="AA" />

In [[382 BBY]]<ref name="HRA1Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 1|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 1]] to [[382 BBY]].</ref> during the [[High Republic Era]], HURID-327 was part of a crowd in the castle's common room that watched the [[Galactic Antipiracy Command|lawman]] [[Raf Thatchburn]] argue with Kanata's employee [[Alak]]. The fight escalatied to violence between the two when the [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Savina Besatrix Malagán|Savina Malagán]] used [[the Force]] to [[Telekinesis|throw]] a cup at Thatchburn, which the lawman assumed had been thrown by Alak. Kanata then arrived and broke up the fight, after which she spotted the [[prospector]] [[Dexter Jettster]] and rushed to hug him, telling Jettster that if he had let her know he was coming, she would have had HURID-327 prepare a tray of the prospector's favorite treats.<ref name="HRA1" />

===Beating from a baby===
{{Quote|I'm going to the pantry to get some milk for him. HURID, can you see if you can get the little guy to stop screaming?''"<br />"''I'm trying, Mistress Maz! Nothing seems to&mdash;oh my!|Maz Kanata and HURID-327, the later of whom is attacked by Qort|<ref name="HR9" />}}
[[File:BabyQortAttack-2021THRA9.png|thumb|right|300px|HURID-327 was attacked by an infant Qort.]]
[[Standard year|Years]] prior to [[231 BBY]],<ref name="HRA9Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the "current" events of [[The High Republic Adventures (2021) 9|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2021) 9]] to [[231 BBY]]. [[Qort]] is depicted as an [[Youngling|adolescent]] in the "current" events, where as he is depicted as an infant during the flashback sequences that HURID-327 appears in, meaning they must have taken place [[Standard year|years]] earlier.</ref> the [[Aloxian]] infant [[Qort]] was delivered to the castle's doorstep with a warning that he was dangerous. Kanata took in the screaming infant and placed him, still in the box that he had been delivered in, on one of the castle's table tops. She then asked HURID-327 to see if it could stop the infant crying while she fetched [[milk]] from the pantry. HURID-327 protested that it was already unsuccessfully trying to calm Qort, but as soon as Kananta left the room, the infant leapt from the box onto the loadlifter's left [[Limb|arm]] and snapped the limb off.<ref name="HR9" />

The mobile baby then procceeded to beat HURID-327 with its own severed arm and reduced the groundskeeper to a pile of still active parts before fleeing to the castle's basement. Kanata eventually returned and discovered the damaged HURID-327, who informed her of where Qort had gone. Kanata found the infant wearing the [[Bone|skull]] of a [[vonduun crab]] that calmed him. After finding the mask, Qort ceased causing destruction, but as HURID-327 tickled the infant on a table in the castle sometime later, the young Aloxian began using the Force to lift small animals around the room, alerting Kanata to the fact that he was [[Force-sensitive]]. Kanata then contacted Malagán about the infant, and Qort left the castle to join the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="HR9" />

===No more grounds to keep===
{{Quote|One look at HURID-327, the groundskeeper at Maz Kanata's castle on Takodana, has inspired plenty of potential visitors to turn right around and head home.|R0-GR|<ref name="Droidography">''[[Star Wars: Droidography]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Hurid-327.png|thumb|left|300px|HURID-327, outside of Maz Kanata's castle.]]
[[Standard century|Centuries]] later in [[34 ABY]],<ref name="TFADate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of {{Film|VII}} to [[34 ABY]].</ref> HURID-327 was still working for Kanata at the castle. While leaving the castle to walk to its [[Starship|ship]],<ref name="Geektionary" /> the loadlifter passed a group consisting of the [[human]]s [[Han Solo]], [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], and [[Finn]], and the [[BB-series astromech droid|astromech droid]] [[BB-8]] as they entered the castle in search of Kanata. Shortly after the group's arrival, the [[First Order]] arrived on Takodana and [[Battle of Takodana|attacked]] the castle while searching for BB-8. The structure was destroyed, but Kanata, the group, and various patrons survived the incident.<ref name="TFA" />

At some point after the castle's destruction, the [[B1-series battle droid]] [[R0-GR]] wrote about HURID-327 in the [[book]] he compiled title "[[droidography]]" and claimed that one look at HURID-327 had caused many potential visitors to Kanata's castle to turn around and head home instead.<ref name="Droidography" /> A mention and illustration of HURID-327 was also included in an [[Unidentified artist|artist's]] [[Unidentified artist's journal|journal]], which was restored, expanded, and displayed by the [[Graf Archive]]<ref name="AA" /> at some point no earlier than 34 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]].<ref name="Year">{{AlienArchiveJournalDate}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
HURID-327 was a simple, older model of loadlifter with [[Color|red]] plating and was able to communicate only via a [[binary]] [[acoustic signaller]],<ref name="BR2D268" /> although this did not prevent the [[droid]] from speaking [[Galactic Basic Standard|Galactic Basic]].<ref name="HR9" /> An oddly jovial droid,<ref name="Hurid-327">{{Databank|hurid-327|Hurid-327}}</ref> he had a gentle sense of humor, but was known to be a little lazy.<ref name="BR2D268" />

HURID-327's tall stature required [[Repulsorlift|repulsor]] supports that generated a counterweight<ref name="Geektionary" /> and the loadlifter had a [[repulsor anchor]] disc mounted on each shoulder. These counterbalances ensured that there was the same weight on both sides of HURID-327's body even when an item he was carrying shifted in transit, which helped the droid luggage porter stay upright when carrying off-balance items.<ref name="BR2D268" /> HURID-327's body core was also [[Gyro stabilizer|gyrostablized]],<ref name="TFAVD" /> as suggested by the high position of its main [[Photoreceptor|receptors]],<ref name="Geektionary" /> which were red in color.<ref name="TFA" />

HURID-327 had reinforced articulation<ref name="Geektionary" /> with two weight-distributing legs and two arms with cargo support joints at the elbows.<ref name="TFAVD" /> Each of his strong, prehensile hands<ref name="Geektionary" /> had three heavy-duty, jointed industrial manipulators fingers and a equally chunky thumb, meaning he rarely lost his grip.<ref name="BR2D268" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Neal said, 'Let's put a stilt-walker in it!' I thought he was mad! [Laughs.] Katy Coleman, the stilt-walker/performer, did a great job inside.|Luke Fisher speaks about Neal Scanlan's reaction to HURID-327|<ref name="Art">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]''</ref>}}
[[File:CastleDroidH027-ArtTFA.png|thumb|right|300px|Castle Droid H027 by Luke Fisher]]
HURID-327 was created to appear in the [[sequel trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']],<ref name="Art" /> which was released on [[December 18]], [[2015]].<ref name="TFA Release">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-episode-vii-to-open-december-18-2015|text=Star Wars: Episode VII to Open December 18, 2015}}</ref> Prior to the film's release, the droid debuted in a trailer for Episode VII on [[October 19]], 2015.<ref name="SWYouTube: Star Wars: The Force Awakens Trailer (Official)">{{SWYouTube|sGbxmsDFVnE|Star Wars: The Force Awakens Trailer (Official)|sw_url=video/star-wars-the-force-awakens-trailer-official}}</ref> Concept art of the character titled "Castle Droid H027" was created by senior sculpter [[Luke Fisher]]<ref name="Art" /> on [[November 26]], [[2013]].<ref name="YouTube">{{SWYouTube|qV_dg8Citm4|The Creatures, Droids and Aliens of Star Wars: The Force Awakens &#124; Star Wars Celebration Europe 2016}}</ref>

Creature creative supervisor [[Neal Scanlan]] suggested that they put a stilt-walker inside the HURID-327 costume and, although Fisher thought the idea was mad,<ref name="Art" /> circus performer<ref name="YouTube" /> [[Katy Coleman]],<ref name="Art" /> who worked under the name "Katy Cartwheel," was picked for the role. The costume was then built around her by the fabricators and the mechanical department in order to ensure that she could move around and see while comfortable and with enough time to create a good performance. During production, the character was known as "Big Red,"<ref name="YouTube" /> with its [[in-universe]] identification of HURID-327 first provided by the reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]]<ref name="TFAVD" /> and released on the same day as the film.<ref name="Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary">{{PenguinRandomHouse|url=books/533307/star-wars-the-force-awakens-the-visual-dictionary-by-pablo-hidalgo|text=Star Wars: The Force Awakens The Visual Dictionary}}</ref>

